{"id":"mahabharata-9-019","work":"mahabharata","part":9,"partName":"शल्यपर्व","partNameEn":"Shalya Parva","unit":19,"title":"एकोनविंशतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 19 · Satyaki kills Shalva","summary":{"en":"Shalva, the leader of the mleccha host, attacks with his great elephant, and the Pandava army breaks before it. Satyaki kills Shalva and his elephant together, and the Panchala prince Dhrishtadyumna revives the troops.","kn":"ಮ್ಲೇಚ್ಛ ಸೈನ್ಯದ ನಾಯಕ ಶಾಲ್ವ ತನ್ನ ಮಹಾಗಜದೊಡನೆ ದಾಳಿ ಮಾಡುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಪಾಂಡವ ಸೈನ್ಯ ಅವನ ಮುಂದೆ ಒಡೆಯುತ್ತದೆ. ಸಾತ್ಯಕಿ ಶಾಲ್ವ ಮತ್ತು ಆನೆಯನ್ನು ಒಟ್ಟಿಗೆ ಕೊಲ್ಲುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಧೃಷ್ಟದ್ಯುಮ್ನ ಸೈನ್ಯವನ್ನು ಉತ್ತೇಜಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"म्लेच्छ सेना का नायक शाल्व अपने विशाल हाथी के साथ आक्रमण करता है और पाण्डव सेना उसके आगे टूट जाती है। सात्यकि शाल्व और हाथी को एक साथ मारता है और धृष्टद्युम्न सैनिकों को फिर उत्साहित करते हैं।","te":"మ్లేచ్ఛ సేన నాయకుడు శాల్వుడు తన మహాగజంతో దాడి చేస్తాడు; పాండవసేన అతని ఎదుట విరిగిపోతుంది. సాత్యకి శాల్వుని, ఏనుగును కలిపి చంపుతాడు; ధృష్టద్యుమ్నుడు సేనను ఉత్తేజపరుస్తాడు.","ta":"ம்லேச்சப் படைத்தலைவன் சால்வன் தன் பெரும் யானையுடன் தாக்க, பாண்டவப் படை அவன் முன் உடைகிறது. சாத்யகி சால்வனையும் யானையையும் சேர்த்துக் கொல்ல, த்ருஷ்டத்யும்னன் வீரரை உற்சாகப்படுத்துகிறான்.","ml":"മ്ലേച്ഛസേനാനായകനായ ശാല്വൻ തന്റെ വലിയ ആനയുമായി ആക്രമിക്കുന്നു; അതിനുമുന്നിൽ പാണ്ഡവസേന ഭഞ്ജിക്കുന്നു. സാത്യകി ശാല്വനെയും അദ്ദേഹത്തിന്റെ ആനയെയും ഒന്നിച്ചു കൊല്ലുന്നു; പാഞ്ചാല രാജകുമാരൻ ധൃഷ്ടദ്യുമ്നൻ സേനയെ ഉണർത്തുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 9.19; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jun 23 2020","sections":[{"title":"शल्यपर्व","titleEn":"Shalya Parva","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"संनिवृत्ते बलौघे तु शाल्वो म्लेच्छगणाधिपः ।\nअभ्यवर्तत संक्रुद्धः पाण्डूनां सुमहद्बलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the flood of troops had turned back, Shalva, lord of the horde of barbarians, furiously attacked the great Pandava army."}},{"n":2,"text":"आस्थाय सुमहानागं प्रभिन्नं पर्वतोपमम् ।\nदृप्तमैरावतप्रख्यममित्रगणमर्दनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He rode a huge rutting elephant, like a mountain, proud as Airavata and a crusher of enemy hosts."}},{"n":3,"text":"योऽसौ महाभद्रकुलप्रसूतः\nसुपूजितो धार्तराष्ट्रेण नित्यम् ।\nसुकल्पितः शास्त्रविनिश्चयज्ञैः\nसदोपवाह्यः समरेषु राजन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That elephant, born in the line of the Mahabhadras, was always honored by Duryodhana, fitted out by men expert in the treatises, and ever used as a mount in battles, O king."}},{"n":4,"text":"तमास्थितो राजवरो बभूव\nयथोदयस्थः सविता क्षपान्ते ।\nस तेन नागप्रवरेण राज-\nन्नभ्युद्ययौ पाण्डुसुतान्समन्तात् ।\nशितैः पृषत्कैर्विददार चापि\nमहेन्द्रवज्रप्रतिमैः सुघोरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mounted on it, that best of kings shone like the sun risen at the end of night. On that finest of elephants, O king, he advanced on the sons of Pandu from every side, tearing them with sharp, dreadful arrows like the thunderbolt of Indra."}},{"n":5,"text":"ततः शरान्वै सृजतो महारणे\nयोधांश्च राजन्नयतो यमाय ।\nनास्यान्तरं ददृशुः स्वे परे वा\nयथा पुरा वज्रधरस्य दैत्याः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he loosed arrows in that great battle and sent warriors to Death, O king, neither his own men nor the enemy could find any opening, as the demons once found none against the wielder of the thunderbolt."}},{"n":6,"text":"ते पाण्डवाः सोमकाः सृञ्जयाश्च\nतमेव नागं ददृशुः समन्तात् ।\nसहस्रशो वै विचरन्तमेकं\nयथा महेन्द्रस्य गजं समीपे ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Pandavas, Somakas and Srinjayas saw that elephant all around them, one animal ranging by the thousand, like the elephant of great Indra close by."}},{"n":7,"text":"संद्राव्यमाणं तु बलं परेषां\nपरीतकल्पं विबभौ समन्तात् ।\nनैवावतस्थे समरे भृशं भया-\nद्विमर्दमानं तु परस्परं तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The enemy army, being driven back, seemed hemmed in on every side; crushed against one another in terror, it could not hold its ground in the battle."}},{"n":8,"text":"ततः प्रभग्ना सहसा महाचमूः\nसा पाण्डवी तेन नराधिपेन ।\nदिशश्चतस्रः सहसा प्रधाविता\nगजेन्द्रवेगं तमपारयन्ती ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the great Pandava army, suddenly broken by that king, fled in the four directions, unable to withstand the elephant's rush."}},{"n":9,"text":"दृष्ट्वा च तां वेगवता प्रभग्नां\nसर्वे त्वदीया युधि योधमुख्याः ।\nअपूजयंस्तत्र नराधिपं तं\nदध्मुश्च शङ्खाञ्शशिसंनिकाशान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing it routed by that fast attacker, all the chief warriors on your side honored that king and blew conches white as the moon."}},{"n":10,"text":"श्रुत्वा निनादं त्वथ कौरवाणां\nहर्षाद्विमुक्तं सह शङ्खशब्दैः ।\nसेनापतिः पाण्डवसृञ्जयानां\nपाञ्चालपुत्रो न ममर्ष रोषात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing the shout of the Kauravas, released with joy and mingled with conch-blasts, the Panchala prince, commander of the Pandavas and Srinjayas, could not bear it in his anger."}},{"n":11,"text":"ततस्तु तं वै द्विरदं महात्मा\nप्रत्युद्ययौ त्वरमाणो जयाय ।\nजम्भो यथा शक्रसमागमे वै\nनागेन्द्रमैरावणमिन्द्रवाह्यम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the great-souled Dhrishtadyumna, eager for victory, hurried against that elephant, as Jambha once met Indra's mount, the king of elephants Airavana, in the fight with Shakra."}},{"n":12,"text":"तमापतन्तं सहसा तु दृष्ट्वा\nपाञ्चालराजं युधि राजसिंहः ।\nतं वै द्विपं प्रेषयामास तूर्णं\nवधाय राजन्द्रुपदात्मजस्य ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the Panchala king's son charge at him suddenly, that lion among kings quickly drove the elephant at him to kill the son of Drupada, O king."}},{"n":13,"text":"स तं द्विपं सहसाभ्यापतन्त-\nमविध्यदर्कप्रतिमैः पृषत्कैः ।\nकर्मारधौतैर्निशितैर्ज्वलद्भि-\nर्नाराचमुख्यैस्त्रिभिरुग्रवेगैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the elephant rushed at him, Dhrishtadyumna pierced it with three fierce, fast, blazing arrows, sharp, smith-polished and bright as the sun, the best of iron shafts."}},{"n":14,"text":"ततोऽपरान्पञ्च शितान्महात्मा\nनाराचमुख्यान्विससर्ज कुम्भे ।\nस तैस्तु विद्धः परमद्विपो रणे\nतदा परावृत्य भृशं प्रदुद्रुवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the great-souled one loosed five more sharp iron arrows at its temple. Struck by these, the mighty elephant turned about in the battle and fled in panic."}},{"n":15,"text":"तं नागराजं सहसा प्रणुन्नं\nविद्राव्यमाणं च निगृह्य शाल्वः ।\nतोत्त्राङ्कुशैः प्रेषयामास तूर्णं\nपाञ्चालराजस्य रथं प्रदिश्य ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shalva, restraining that king of elephants, pushed back and routed, drove it quickly with goad and hook, pointing it toward the chariot of the Panchala prince."}},{"n":16,"text":"दृष्ट्वापतन्तं सहसा तु नागं\nधृष्टद्युम्नः स्वरथाच्छीघ्रमेव ।\nगदां प्रगृह्याशु जवेन वीरो\nभूमिं प्रपन्नो भयविह्वलाङ्गः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the elephant bearing down on him, the hero Dhrishtadyumna quickly took a mace and leapt from his chariot to the ground, his limbs shaking with fear."}},{"n":17,"text":"स तं रथं हेमविभूषिताङ्गं\nसाश्वं ससूतं सहसा विमृद्य ।\nउत्क्षिप्य हस्तेन तदा महाद्विपो\nविपोथयामास वसुंधरातले ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great elephant crushed that chariot, its body adorned with gold, with its horses and charioteer, and, lifting it with its trunk, smashed it to the ground."}},{"n":18,"text":"पाञ्चालराजस्य सुतं स दृष्ट्वा\nतदार्दितं नागवरेण तेन ।\nतमभ्यधावत्सहसा जवेन\nभीमः शिखण्डी च शिनेश्च नप्ता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the Panchala king's son beset by that fine elephant, Bhima, Shikhandi and the grandson of Shini rushed at it swiftly."}},{"n":19,"text":"शरैश्च वेगं सहसा निगृह्य\nतस्याभितोऽभ्यापततो गजस्य ।\nस संगृहीतो रथिभिर्गजो वै\nचचाल तैर्वार्यमाणश्च संख्ये ॥","meaning":{"en":"They checked the rushing elephant's speed with arrows from every side, and the elephant, held by the chariot-warriors, wavered as they resisted it in battle."}},{"n":20,"text":"ततः पृषत्कान्प्रववर्ष राजा\nसूर्यो यथा रश्मिजालं समन्तात् ।\nतेनाशुगैर्वध्यमाना रथौघाः\nप्रदुद्रुवुस्तत्र ततस्तु सर्वे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then King Shalva rained arrows on every side as the sun spreads a net of rays. Struck by his swift shafts, the masses of chariots all fled."}},{"n":21,"text":"तत्कर्म शाल्वस्य समीक्ष्य सर्वे\nपाञ्चालमत्स्या नृप सृञ्जयाश्च ।\nहाहाकारैर्नादयन्तः स्म युद्धे\nद्विपं समन्ताद्रुरुधुर्नराग्र्याः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Shalva's deed, all the Panchalas, Matsyas and Srinjayas, O king, filled the battle with cries of alarm, and those foremost men hemmed in the elephant on every side."}},{"n":22,"text":"पाञ्चालराजस्त्वरितस्तु शूरो\nगदां प्रगृह्याचलशृङ्गकल्पाम् ।\nअसंभ्रमं भारत शत्रुघाती\nजवेन वीरोऽनुससार नागम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The brave Panchala king's son, killer of foes, took a mace like a mountain peak and, unflustered, O Bharata, followed the elephant quickly."}},{"n":23,"text":"ततोऽथ नागं धरणीधराभं\nमदं स्रवन्तं जलदप्रकाशम् ।\nगदां समाविध्य भृशं जघान\nपाञ्चालराजस्य सुतस्तरस्वी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the swift son of the Panchala king whirled his mace and struck hard the elephant, big as a mountain, streaming rut, looking like a cloud."}},{"n":24,"text":"स भिन्नकुम्भः सहसा विनद्य\nमुखात्प्रभूतं क्षतजं विमुञ्चन् ।\nपपात नागो धरणीधराभः\nक्षितिप्रकम्पाच्चलितो यथाद्रिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With its temple smashed, the elephant suddenly bellowed and, vomiting much blood from its mouth, fell like a mountain shaken loose by an earthquake."}},{"n":25,"text":"निपात्यमाने तु तदा गजेन्द्रे\nहाहाकृते तव पुत्रस्य सैन्ये ।\nस शाल्वराजस्य शिनिप्रवीरो\nजहार भल्लेन शिरः शितेन ॥","meaning":{"en":"As that king of elephants was falling and your son's army cried out in dismay, the hero of the Shini line, Satyaki, cut off Shalva's head with a sharp broad-headed arrow."}},{"n":26,"text":"हृतोत्तमाङ्गो युधि सात्वतेन\nपपात भूमौ सह नागराज्ञा ।\nयथाद्रिशृङ्गं सुमहत्प्रणुन्नं\nवज्रेण देवाधिपचोदितेन ॥","meaning":{"en":"His head struck off in battle by the Satvata, Shalva fell to the ground with the elephant king, like a great mountain peak hurled down by the thunderbolt flung by the lord of the gods."}}]}]}